module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.closure_emit_renders_an_arrow_without_its_body

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data closure_emit_renders_an_arrow_without_its_body: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "closure_emit_renders_an_arrow_without_its_body" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the v2 closure emitter (v2.compiler.self_host.compiler_closure_emit emit_compiler_import_closure_from_ingest, the route v2.cli.compile_cli emits through) reports Accepted and returns text in which a module is a record of its members and a member Arrow is rendered as its domain and codomain with NO BODY** (INVALID STATE: `fn add(x: Int, y: Int) -> Int { x + y }` emits `add: ( { x: i32, y: i32 }) -> (i32) -> i32`, and `data native_cli_door_probe_value: Int = 606060` emits `native_cli_door_probe_value: ( {  }) -> (i32) -> i32`. The `x + y` and the `606060` appear nowhere in the output, and no diagnostic of any severity is carried).",

    "HARM. An Accepted emission that has lost every body is a silent wrong answer, below the ordinary compiler floor (DESIGN section 4b). The emitted text is not a Rust crate, and nothing that reads the door's exit status can tell. `//gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli` admits its emit arm on exit 0 plus the declaration's NAME in the emitted text. That is what the flip instruction asked for, and it is green over this loss. So a green on that arm establishes that the door parsed, resolved, inferred, grounded and translated the fixture, and establishes nothing about the value.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is not `call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering`. There, the body is lost before resolve, in normalize. Here, the inferred tree still carries the body under `arrow_body_edge`: v2.test.execution.data_decl_lowering_grounding data_decl_lowers_to_a_nullary_named_member_holds reads the literal atom at that edge on the resolved tree, and translate's grounding gate walks it. The loss is at rendering. Found 2026-09-23 while lowering `data` declarations for gen-one's door probe, by running the same emit route interpretively over `fn add` on HEAD and on the change: both drop the body, so the class predates that change.",

    "WHERE THE BODY WAS DROPPED (chain re-derivation, DESIGN section 6b), gunbc#12207. The Rust target carries a type-expression projection, so `v2.compiler.translate` `translate_node_with_projection` routes the module root through `translate_type_expression_tree`, which checks for a bodied arrow only at the root and otherwise type-projects the whole subtree. The member arrow reached `translate_type_expression_arrow_project`, which reads only the positional parameter and result children, so the `arrow_body_edge` was discarded by that link's own contract -- the earliest unjustified boundary. The record rendering of the module is the same subtree's fallback: `translate_type_expression_tree` type-projects any node no grammar relation row matches, widening where it should refuse.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder (silent). gunbc#12207 raised it to 1: `translate_type_expression_arrow_project` refuses an arrow carrying an `arrow_body_edge` with `translate_arrow_body_not_a_type_expression`, located at the arrow, and the door pinned that refusal.",

    "RENDERED, AND THE FALLBACK REFUSES (gen-two blocker #4, next rung). The closure-emit path now routes a module to the one module authority, `v2.compiler.emit_produced` `emit_produced_module`, which renders each member through the Rust target's declared rows -- the same `rust_produced_decl_render_rows` the self-host candidate reads -- and projects each body through `target_project_arrow_body_to_value_expression`. The route is taken in `v2.compiler.program_partition` `emit_partition_with_target` only when `produced_module_declares_bodied_members` holds: every member of every module body the dag language authority marks (`namespace_graft_node_is_module_body`) is a bodied declaration. The whole-body condition is load-bearing: the declaration collector skips a member that is not an arrow, and measured on this change a module declaring `type Pair { a: Int, b: Int }` beside `fn add` emitted `fn add` ALONE until the condition was added -- this class again, one member over. The condition is also per body and requires at least one real member: every grafted body carries the production marker, so a raw-children check held vacuously for `module empty` and the fold published zero bytes as an Accepted program (found in review of gunbc#12239); a declarationless body now refuses like the others. A module that fails it reaches `translate_type_expression_tree`, which now refuses `translate_module_not_a_type_expression` located at the module body instead of type-projecting it as a record. Rendering `606060` needed a general integer literal: the value projection spelled only magnitudes 1 and 2, through legacy binding rows, so `TargetValueExprIntLiteral` renders any other magnitude through the target's declared `int_literal_form`, Rust's being `rust_token_int_literal`, the class its lexer reads the literal with on ingest.",

    "RUNG NOW, PER PATH (DESIGN section 4b(1)). CLOSURE-EMIT PATH (`emit_compiler_import_closure_from_ingest`, which `v2.cli.compile_cli` emits through): 3, structurally guaranteed -- an Accepted emission of a module has rendered every member's body through the rows, and every other module is refused by the compiler on the acceptance path, typed and located. Executed evidence, run interpretively over this change: `v2.test.emit.closure_emit_arrow_body_refusal` -- `fn add` emits `fn add(x: i32, y: i32) -> i32 { x + y }`, and the module adding `type Pair` refuses `translate_module_not_a_type_expression` in the authored file; with the route disabled the two rendering rows are false and the refusal rows hold. The door's fold over the fixture's module and declaration emits `fn native_cli_door_probe_value() -> i32 { 606060 }`, which rustc accepts. SELF-HOST CANDIDATE PATH (`v2.compiler.self_host.candidate_generation` `generate_rust_module_emission_candidate`): NOT RAISED -- it calls `emit_produced_module` over `produced_decl_conjs_in_tree` without the whole-body condition, so a non-arrow member there is skipped rather than refused; unmeasured in this change, so the class's current rung is that path's, below 3.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: the self-host candidate path admits a module only when `produced_module_declares_bodied_members` holds, or renders every member kind it admits, so no member is skipped on either emission path. Separately, the door stays short of whole modules with type declarations until the Rust target's rows render a type declaration; until then such a module refuses, which is honest and not this class.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.translate", decl_name: "translate_type_expression_arrow_project", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.translate", decl_name: "translate_type_expression_tree", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.emit_produced", decl_name: "produced_module_declares_bodied_members", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.program_partition", decl_name: "emit_partition_with_target", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.emit.closure_emit_arrow_body_refusal", decl_name: "a_function_body_is_rendered_with_its_declaration_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.emit.closure_emit_arrow_body_refusal", decl_name: "the_rendered_function_is_a_rust_item_not_a_record_field_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.emit.closure_emit_arrow_body_refusal", decl_name: "a_module_the_rows_cannot_render_whole_refuses_rather_than_dropping_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.emit.closure_emit_arrow_body_refusal", decl_name: "the_module_refusal_is_located_in_the_authored_file_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
